import Mathlib

/-! Blind readings A, B, C (code unchanged; only `import Mathlib` hoisted). -/

-- ===== reader A =====

namespace ReaderA

open MeasureTheory Pointwise

/-- A convex body in `ℝⁿ`: a compact convex set with nonempty interior. -/
def IsConvexBody {n : ℕ} (K : Set (Fin n → ℝ)) : Prop :=
  Convex ℝ K ∧ IsCompact K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty

/-- The lattice `Λ = A ℤⁿ` generated by the columns of the matrix `A`. When `det A ≠ 0` this is
a full-rank lattice, and every full-rank lattice in `ℝⁿ` is of this form. -/
def latticeOf {n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) : Set (Fin n → ℝ) :=
  Set.range fun z : Fin n → ℤ => A.mulVec (fun i => (z i : ℝ))

/-- Theorem 1.1: there is an absolute constant `C > 0` such that for every integer `n ≥ 2` and
every convex body `K ⊂ ℝⁿ` some full-rank lattice `Λ = A ℤⁿ` (`det A ≠ 0`) satisfies
`K + Λ = ℝⁿ` and `vol_n(K) / det Λ ≤ C n log n`, where `det Λ = |det A|` is the covolume.
The inequality is stated multiplied out, `vol_n(K) ≤ C n log n · |det A|`, in `ℝ≥0∞`. -/
theorem reading_thm_1_1 :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, 2 ≤ n → ∀ K : Set (Fin n → ℝ), IsConvexBody K →
      ∃ A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ, A.det ≠ 0 ∧
        K + latticeOf A = Set.univ ∧
        volume K ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (C * n * Real.log n * |A.det|) := by
  sorry

end ReaderA

/-
Ambiguities and choices.

1. ℝⁿ: `Fin n → ℝ` with Mathlib's `volume` (product Lebesgue measure = n-dimensional Lebesgue
   measure vol_n). Its topology (sup norm) is the Euclidean topology, so "compact" and
   "interior" are the usual ones; `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` would give the same statement.
2. Convex body: the source's definition "compact with nonempty interior" plus convexity:
   `Convex ℝ K ∧ IsCompact K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty`. No symmetry or regularity assumed.
3. Full-rank lattice Λ and det Λ: written by hand as Λ = A ℤⁿ with A an n×n real matrix,
   det A ≠ 0, and det Λ = |det A| (the covolume, i.e. the volume of the fundamental
   parallelepiped). This is independent of the choice of basis and every full-rank lattice
   (discrete subgroup spanning ℝⁿ) arises so; it is equivalent to Mathlib's `IsZLattice` with
   `ZLattice.covolume`. I quantify over A rather than over Λ to avoid defining covolume as a
   function of a set.
4. K + Λ = ℝⁿ: pointwise Minkowski sum of sets `K + latticeOf A = Set.univ`.
5. vol(K)/det Λ ≤ C n log n: multiplied out as vol(K) ≤ C n log n · |det A| (|det A| > 0, so
   equivalent), and kept in ℝ≥0∞ via `ENNReal.ofReal`, so no `toReal` of a possibly infinite
   measure and no division (vol(K) is finite anyway since K is compact). For n ≥ 2,
   log n ≥ log 2 > 0, so the right side is a genuine positive real; log is natural (Real.log).
6. "absolute constant C > 0": ∃ C quantified before n and K. "one full-rank lattice" read as
   "some (at least one)" lattice.
7. The infimum θ_L(K) in the definition is not needed for Theorem 1.1 as stated (it would
   follow as θ_L(K) ≤ C n log n); I state the theorem's explicit lattice form, avoiding an
   `sInf`.
-/

-- ===== reader B =====

open scoped Pointwise
namespace ReaderB

/-- Convex body: compact, convex, nonempty interior. -/
def IsConvexBody {n : ℕ} (K : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) : Prop :=
  Convex ℝ K ∧ IsCompact K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty

/-- Theorem 1.1. Lattices are discrete `ℤ`-submodules spanning `ℝⁿ`; `det Λ` is `ZLattice.covolume`. -/
theorem reading_latticecov_main :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, 2 ≤ n → ∀ K : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)), IsConvexBody K →
      ∃ (Λ : Submodule ℤ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (_ : DiscreteTopology Λ) (_ : IsZLattice ℝ Λ),
        K + (Λ : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) = Set.univ ∧
        (MeasureTheory.volume K).toReal / ZLattice.covolume Λ ≤ C * n * Real.log n := sorry

/-
Ambiguities / choices:
* ℝⁿ is EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) with Lebesgue `volume`; "full-rank lattice" = discrete ℤ-submodule with
  IsZLattice ℝ (spans over ℝ, hence rank n). det Λ = ZLattice.covolume Λ (volume of a fundamental domain).
* vol_n(K) = (volume K).toReal: K compact so volume is finite, no toReal-of-∞ junk. Covolume is positive
  for a full-rank lattice, so the division is genuine.
* Convex body = convex ∧ compact ∧ nonempty interior. K + Λ is the pointwise Minkowski sum of sets.
* log n with n ≥ 2 is positive (natural log); no junk. C is real, n cast to ℝ.
* The theorem states existence of one Λ per K (not the infimum θ_L), matching Theorem 1.1 literally.
-/
end ReaderB

-- ===== reader C =====

namespace ReaderC

open scoped Pointwise

/-- A convex body in ℝⁿ: compact, convex, with nonempty interior (the text's convention). -/
def IsConvexBody {n : ℕ} (K : Set (Fin n → ℝ)) : Prop :=
  IsCompact K ∧ Convex ℝ K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty

/-- The lattice Λ generated by the vectors b_0,…,b_{n-1} ∈ ℝⁿ: their ℤ-span. When the b_i
are linearly independent over ℝ (n of them in ℝⁿ, so a basis) this is a full-rank lattice. -/
def latticeOf {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → (Fin n → ℝ)) : AddSubgroup (Fin n → ℝ) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range b)

/-- The covolume det Λ of the lattice with basis b (rows b_i): |det(b_i j)|. -/
noncomputable def covol {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → (Fin n → ℝ)) : ℝ :=
  |Matrix.det (Matrix.of b)|

/-- Theorem 1.1: there is an absolute C > 0 such that for every n ≥ 2 and every convex body
K ⊂ ℝⁿ there is a full-rank lattice Λ with K + Λ = ℝⁿ and vol(K)/det Λ ≤ C n log n.
The lattice is produced as `latticeOf b` for a linearly independent family b. -/
theorem reading_latticecov_main :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, 2 ≤ n → ∀ K : Set (Fin n → ℝ), IsConvexBody K →
      ∃ b : Fin n → (Fin n → ℝ), LinearIndependent ℝ b ∧
        K + (latticeOf b : Set (Fin n → ℝ)) = Set.univ ∧
        (MeasureTheory.volume K).toReal / covol b ≤ C * (n : ℝ) * Real.log (n : ℝ) := sorry

/-
Ambiguities and choices (reader C):

1. Lattice: "full-rank lattice" is read as the ℤ-span of an ℝ-basis of ℝⁿ, i.e. a discrete
   subgroup of full rank. Since n independent vectors in ℝⁿ form a basis, requiring
   `LinearIndependent ℝ b` with b : Fin n → ℝⁿ encodes exactly full rank; discreteness is
   automatic. Every full-rank lattice has such a generating family, so the existential
   over b is not weaker than the existential over lattices.
2. Covolume: det Λ is |det| of the basis matrix (rows b_i). It is independent of the chosen
   basis, and it is nonzero because b is a basis, so the division is well defined.
3. Convex body: compact, convex, nonempty interior (the text's stated convention). No
   symmetry or boundary regularity is assumed, as in the text.
4. vol_n: `MeasureTheory.volume` on Fin n → ℝ (product Lebesgue measure). K is compact, so
   its volume is finite and `.toReal` loses nothing. (ENNReal.toReal would be junk at ⊤,
   which cannot occur here.)
5. Translates: K + Λ is the pointwise sum of the set K with the subgroup Λ coerced to a set
   (`open scoped Pointwise`); the covering condition is equality with Set.univ.
6. The bound C n log n: the text's log is natural. For n ≥ 2, log n ≥ log 2 > 0, so the
   bound is nontrivial and no junk from log of small arguments arises (n = 1 is excluded
   by the hypothesis 2 ≤ n, as in the text).
7. The constant C > 0 is an existential absolute constant (not specified), as in the text.
8. Real.log and ℕ-to-ℝ casts: n is cast to ℝ explicitly in both places, so no ℕ subtraction
   or ℕ-division appears in the statement.
-/

end ReaderC
